 "title": "Build a Viral Instagram Page Using 59 Styles",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "The creator explains how to use a free GitHub toolbox called lemo-opuscar with Claude Code to generate daily videos across 59 film styles. By sticking to one style and one topic and posting every day, you can grow your Instagram page.",
 "key_points": [
  "Use the free toolbox lemo-opuscar on GitHub, which provides 59 film styles for Claude Code.",
  "Step 1: Install it by pasting two lines into Claude Code (requires Node 20+, ffmpeg, and Python 3.11+).",
  "Step 2: Pick one style that fits your page (e.g., Watercolor, Crayon Picture Book, 16-bit Pixel RPG, Ukiyo-e, Mid-century Cartoon, Tilt-Shift Miniature).",
  "Step 3: Tell Claude a style and a story, and it will draw it, add music, and narrate it in about 30 to 60 minutes per film.",
  "Step 4: Stick to one style and one topic, and post every day.",
  "Do not mix all 59 styles on one page, otherwise people will not know what your page is about."
 ],
 "content": "Claude, I'm starting a new Instagram page. I want to go viral and make money! With what videos? There's a free toolbox. Fifty-nine kinds of videos. Watch. Step one. Lemo Opuscar. Paste two lines into Claude Code. Just two lines? Two, I counted for you. Step two. Pick the look that fits your page. Watercolor, calm stories, travel. Crayon picture book, kids' stories, parents share these. Pixel game, gaming pages, life recaps. Japanese woodblock, history, myths. Fifties cartoon, how-to guides. Tiny toy city, satisfying city scenes. Which one goes viral? The one you post every day. Not the one you post once. Step three. Give me a style and a story. I draw it, add music, and narrate it. How long does it take? About an hour. You're good at that. Go eat. Step four. One style, one topic. Post every day. That's your page. Can I use all fifty-nine on one page? Nobody knows what your page is. Pick one. Commit. I know. New for you. So which style is me? Crayon book. Simple, colorful, a little confused. Which style would your page be? Comment FILM for all 59 styles + prompts. Follow for the next one. Text shown on screen: Get the toolbox (github.com/lemo-ai/lemo-opuscar, 59 film styles, free MIT, 6.6k); Step one. Lemo Opuscar; Terminal: claude; claude plugin marketplace add lemo-ai/lemo-opuscar (marketplace added: lemolab), claude plugin install lemo-opuscar@lemolab (installed lemo-opuscar, installed lamo-opuscar, Needs Node 20+ ffmpeg Python 3.11+); Installed 2 counted; Step two. Pick your look (50 styles, 59 styles); Watercolor brush (good for: Travel, Calm stories); Crayon Picture Book (good for: Kids' stories); 16-bit Pixel RPG (good for: Gaming, Recaps); Ukiyo-e (good for: History, Myths); Mid-century Cartoon (good for: How-to guides); Tilt-Shift Miniature (good for: Satisfying); Which one goes viral? The one you post every day, Not the one you post once; Step three. Tell me the story; Claude Code: lemo-opuscar; Make a 45-second vertical (1080x1920) film in the watercolor style. A lost dog finds his way home; Drawing done, Music done, Narration done; result watercolor 0:45; ~30-60 min per film; Step four. Post and grow; @slow.watercolor (0 posts, 15 followers, 1 following, Can't have stories, pained, Follow); One style: Watercolor, One topic: calm travel, Post every day (day 6 / 30); @slow.watercolor (15 posts, 1528 followers, 14 following, Follow); One style: Watercolor, One topic: calm travel, Post every day (day 24 / 30), 1,528 Followers; Full guide: every prompt; @slow.watercolor (45 posts, 2,480 followers, 15 following, Follow); One style: Watercolor, One topic: calm travel, Post every day (day 30 / 30), 2,480 Followers; what is this page?; Crayon Picture Book (Ash's style: To eat small fish, not to be full, and sleep); Which style would your page be? Comment FILM for all 59 styles + prompts. Follow for the next one.",
